@MiniErp.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5014

# Validation scenarios from specs/001-gestion-clientes/quickstart.md, section 2.

### 1. Create a customer (US1-1): 201 with Location; taxId normalized to 20123456786
# @name createCustomer
POST {{MiniErp.Api_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "legalName": "Pérez, Juan",
  "taxId": "20-12345678-6",
  "vatCondition": "finalConsumer",
  "email": "juan@example.com",
  "phone": "+54 11 4321-5678",
  "address": "Av. Siempre Viva 742"
}

### 2. Same tax id without separators (US1-2): 409 "Customer already exists"
POST {{MiniErp.Api_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "legalName": "Pérez, Juan",
  "taxId": "20123456786",
  "vatCondition": "finalConsumer"
}

### 3. Several invalid fields (US1-3, US1-4): one 400 with taxId, email and legalName
POST {{MiniErp.Api_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "taxId": "20-12345678-5",
  "vatCondition": "finalConsumer",
  "email": "foo"
}

### 4. List customers (US2-1): 200, ordered by legal name, with totalCount
GET {{MiniErp.Api_HostAddress}}/api/customers

### 5. Page size over the maximum (FR-005): 400 with an error on pageSize
GET {{MiniErp.Api_HostAddress}}/api/customers?pageSize=101

### 6. Customer detail (US2-2): 200 with all the data (uses the id created in request 1)
GET {{MiniErp.Api_HostAddress}}/api/customers/{{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}

### 7. Unknown customer (US2-3): 404
GET {{MiniErp.Api_HostAddress}}/api/customers/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000

### 8. Replace all data without phone (US3-1, US3-5): 200 and "phone": null (uses the id from request 1)
PUT {{MiniErp.Api_HostAddress}}/api/customers/{{createCustomer.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "legalName": "Pérez, Juan Carlos",
  "taxId": "20-12345678-6",
  "vatCondition": "registeredTaxpayer",
  "email": "juancarlos@example.com",
  "address": "Calle Falsa 123"
}
